{title: Like a Tree by the Water}
{subtitle: Psalm 1}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Blessed is the one who does not [Eb]walk in the counsel of the wic[Bb]ked
Who does not stand in the way of [Eb]sinners
Who does not sit in the seat of mock[Gm]ers
But whose delight is in the in[Eb]struction of the LORD
And who [F]murmurs over his instruction [Eb]day and [Bb]night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He is like a tree transplanted [Eb]beside channels of wa[Bb]ter
Yielding its fruit in season, [Eb]its leaf never withering
In all that he [Gm]does, he [Eb]thrives
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Not so the wic[Gm]ked
They are like [F]chaff that the wind blows a[Bb]way
Therefore the wicked will not [Eb]stand in the judgment
Nor [F]sinners in the assembly of the right[Eb]eous
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
For the LORD knows the [Gm]way of the right[F]eous
But the [Eb]way of the wicked will [Bb]perish
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [Bb] |
